1
00:01:18,100 --> 00:01:19,500
Oh

2
00:01:42,080 --> 00:01:43,417
See you

3
00:01:43,500 --> 00:01:49,400
next time.

4
00:01:50,040 --> 00:01:51,860
Aaaaaaah!

5
00:02:03,040 --> 00:02:04,440
Aaaaaaah!

6
00:02:06,080 --> 00:02:07,960
Aaaaah! Aaaaaaah!

7
00:02:08,980 --> 00:02:09,810
Seeking!

8
00:02:09,893 --> 00:02:10,740
Exists!

9
00:02:16,020 --> 00:02:16,850
Ooh!

10
00:02:27,060 --> 00:02:28,920
Watch out, Iceberg!

11
00:02:34,360 --> 00:02:35,190
Hey!

12
00:02:35,273 --> 00:02:37,119
What in the hell is wrong with you?

13
00:02:44,300 --> 00:02:45,130
Ow! Idiot!

14
00:02:45,220 --> 00:02:47,497
Don't you know you're not supposed
to be goofing around right now?

15
00:02:47,580 --> 00:02:50,237
We got real ships to work
on, not your crappy toys.

16
00:02:50,320 --> 00:02:52,797
Don't yell at me when you don't have
a clue what you're talking about,

17
00:02:52,880 --> 00:02:53,762
ice for brains.

18
00:02:53,920 --> 00:02:55,277
It isn't some crappy toy.

19
00:02:55,360 --> 00:02:57,637
It's my super battleship
that battled Franky.

20
00:02:57,720 --> 00:03:00,677
Whatever it is, you need to leave
it alone before someone gets hurt.

21
00:03:00,760 --> 00:03:02,348
This is Scrap Heave Island.

22
00:03:02,500 --> 00:03:03,760
I can do what I want.

23
00:03:03,960 --> 00:03:04,960
Wait, you'll see.

24
00:03:05,140 --> 00:03:08,377
I'm going to build a battleship
awesome enough to take down a Sea King.

25
00:03:08,460 --> 00:03:10,837
Bull, what you're going to
do is get yourself killed.

26
00:03:10,920 --> 00:03:14,180
Oh, yeah? Yeah, quick. Nuh-uh. Real quick.

27
00:03:17,580 --> 00:03:22,340
If you want to be a man, show some gusto.

28
00:03:40,480 --> 00:03:43,100
Well, there's the old launching ceremony.

29
00:03:43,400 --> 00:03:45,677
One more ship sailing with gusto.

30
00:03:45,760 --> 00:03:47,800
Ha, ha, ha! Right, buddy?

31
00:03:48,020 --> 00:03:49,373
Giddle, giddle, giddle.

32
00:03:49,520 --> 00:03:51,579
That's about enough work for today.

33
00:03:51,860 --> 00:03:53,657
What do you say we head on home?

34
00:03:53,740 --> 00:03:54,617
Giddle, giddle.

35
00:03:54,700 --> 00:03:57,260
Man, I'm hungry. Giddle, giddle.

36
00:03:57,360 --> 00:03:59,007
Let's see what's for dinner.

37
00:03:59,140 --> 00:04:00,022
Giddle, giddle.

38
00:04:00,420 --> 00:04:02,040
Hey, hold on!

39
00:04:02,280 --> 00:04:03,320
Wait for us!

40
00:04:10,820 --> 00:04:14,680
So today's Battle Franky model
was number, what are you up to?

41
00:04:15,220 --> 00:04:16,050
Ain't, sir.

42
00:04:16,133 --> 00:04:18,580
It was really beautiful. No, it wasn't.

43
00:04:18,760 --> 00:04:20,837
Your dumb weapon that he let
you build for some reason

44
00:04:20,920 --> 00:04:23,517
fell apart after you almost
killed both of us with it.

45
00:04:23,600 --> 00:04:25,717
Nobody asked you, you
stupid ice for brains.

46
00:04:25,800 --> 00:04:27,000
Ice for brains?

47
00:04:27,160 --> 00:04:28,360
Well, you're flunky!

48
00:04:32,760 --> 00:04:35,940
All right, that's enough
fighting, boys. Cut it out.

49
00:04:36,140 --> 00:04:37,700
He started it, not me.

50
00:04:38,980 --> 00:04:39,940
My word.

51
00:04:40,700 --> 00:04:42,600
Don't encourage those two, Tom.

52
00:04:42,820 --> 00:04:43,777
Was it that funny?

53
00:04:43,860 --> 00:04:44,690
Keep laughing.

54
00:04:44,773 --> 00:04:46,277
And they'll keep misbehaving.

55
00:04:46,360 --> 00:04:47,772
Speaking of misbehaving,

56
00:04:47,900 --> 00:04:51,417
I heard that another ship carrying
lumber was attacked by pirates.

57
00:04:51,500 --> 00:04:54,853
I swear, ever since the king
of the pirates was executed,

58
00:04:54,980 --> 00:04:58,017
this place has just gone
rotten with those Newgate bums.

59
00:04:58,100 --> 00:04:59,717
They're taking over the city.

60
00:04:59,800 --> 00:05:01,918
The people's spirits are really low.

61
00:05:02,380 --> 00:05:05,117
And because of all the
flooding from Aqualaguna,

62
00:05:05,200 --> 00:05:08,637
we can only get lumber and iron if
we ship them in from other islands.

63
00:05:08,720 --> 00:05:12,257
But with all the storms and pirates
everywhere, it's near impossible.

64
00:05:12,340 --> 00:05:15,917
The shipyards are starting to
get so desperate for customers,

65
00:05:16,000 --> 00:05:18,677
they are literally fighting
each other for them.

66
00:05:18,760 --> 00:05:20,701
So many have closed down already.

67
00:05:20,860 --> 00:05:21,780
At this rate,

68
00:05:21,920 --> 00:05:26,567
Water 7 is on a course to sink into the
ocean and fade from the world's memory.

69
00:05:26,980 --> 00:05:30,097
And to think, this city made
its name, making unforgettable,

70
00:05:30,180 --> 00:05:32,377
unsinkable ships such a shame.

71
00:05:32,460 --> 00:05:36,537
Hey, you built a big, super awesome
pirate ship once now, didn't you, Tom?

72
00:05:36,620 --> 00:05:40,032
Will you teach me how to draw
out blueprints for one, too?

73
00:05:42,340 --> 00:05:43,575
What's so funny, huh?

74
00:05:44,540 --> 00:05:48,460
Franky, there's no such thing
as blueprints for a pirate ship.

75
00:05:49,000 --> 00:05:50,780
It's the flag, boy.

76
00:05:51,120 --> 00:05:55,780
Skull and bones means pirate ship,
and a Skull flag means that it's navy.

77
00:05:56,320 --> 00:05:59,060
Whatever you build, just remember this.

78
00:05:59,420 --> 00:06:00,900
Build it with pride.

79
00:06:01,280 --> 00:06:03,960
And a whole lot of manly gusto!

80
00:06:08,360 --> 00:06:10,360
You sure are working late tonight.

81
00:06:11,040 --> 00:06:12,275
What are you drawing?

82
00:06:13,380 --> 00:06:15,980
This here is hope for our island

83
00:06:16,880 --> 00:06:18,697
It is? Yep.

84
00:06:18,780 --> 00:06:22,721
Well, at least that's what I'm
hoping that it'll turn into someday!

85
00:06:23,440 --> 00:06:24,737
Now, to bed with ya.

86
00:06:24,820 --> 00:06:26,120
Yes, sir.

87
00:06:32,760 --> 00:06:33,590
Huh?

88
00:06:41,520 --> 00:06:42,380
Whoa! Whoa.

89
00:06:46,600 --> 00:06:48,380
The judicial ship is here.

90
00:06:49,060 --> 00:06:50,440
What the heck is that?

91
00:06:50,940 --> 00:06:52,140
A mobile court.

92
00:06:52,460 --> 00:06:54,225
I wonder who they're here for.

93
00:06:59,500 --> 00:07:01,077
What do you think you're doing?

94
00:07:01,160 --> 00:07:03,160
Let him go, you big stupid jerk.

95
00:07:03,320 --> 00:07:04,697
He didn't do anything wrong.

96
00:07:04,780 --> 00:07:05,721
Don't you worry.

97
00:07:05,940 --> 00:07:07,460
I'll be just fine.

98
00:07:11,180 --> 00:07:12,100
No, Tom!

99
00:07:12,380 --> 00:07:13,320
Come back!

100
00:07:21,620 --> 00:07:26,037
Justice was brought to Gold Roger, the
king of the pirates, by way of execution.

101
00:07:26,120 --> 00:07:27,700
His ship, the Oro Jackson,

102
00:07:27,940 --> 00:07:31,517
was built by none other than Tom,
who stands before this court today.

103
00:07:31,600 --> 00:07:34,317
As penalty for aiding and
abetting that vicious criminal,

104
00:07:34,400 --> 00:07:37,988
Tom will be taken to Ennie's
lobby where he will be executed.

105
00:07:38,700 --> 00:07:39,530
No.

106
00:07:40,040 --> 00:07:42,240
The verdict was read. Guilty.

107
00:07:42,560 --> 00:07:44,266
They're going to execute Tom.

108
00:07:45,060 --> 00:07:48,697
They say it's because he built a
ship for the king of the pirates.

109
00:07:48,780 --> 00:07:49,610
Damn shame.

110
00:07:49,780 --> 00:07:53,015
That thing brought a whole
lot of grief into the world.

111
00:07:53,320 --> 00:07:55,197
Now, building ships is not a crime,

112
00:07:55,280 --> 00:07:58,477
and one may sell them to almost
anyone who wishes to buy,

113
00:07:58,560 --> 00:08:01,277
but we must make an exception
for the king of the pirates.

114
00:08:01,360 --> 00:08:03,917
On the charge of providing
meaningful assistance

115
00:08:04,000 --> 00:08:06,680
to the man who terrorized
the entire world,

116
00:08:06,880 --> 00:08:09,020
we hereby sentence Tom to death.

117
00:08:09,460 --> 00:08:10,500
Take him away.

118
00:08:11,900 --> 00:08:13,780
Come on, time to go. Move it.

119
00:08:13,920 --> 00:08:14,750
You heard him.

120
00:08:15,040 --> 00:08:15,870
Hurry up.

121
00:08:15,980 --> 00:08:16,880
Go already.

122
00:08:17,080 --> 00:08:18,377
Hey, what are you doing?

123
00:08:18,460 --> 00:08:23,340
I've got a new design for a
completely new kind of paddle steamer.

124
00:08:23,500 --> 00:08:27,088
A train that will run on the
surface of the ocean with gusto.

125
00:08:27,720 --> 00:08:29,520
Shut up. Get moving.

126
00:08:30,440 --> 00:08:33,160
This once great island has lost its gusto.

127
00:08:33,480 --> 00:08:35,598
Our trade is not what it used to be.

128
00:08:35,800 --> 00:08:37,160
People have lost hope.

129
00:08:37,980 --> 00:08:40,360
Water 7 is slowly sinking away.

130
00:08:41,020 --> 00:08:44,491
Every day, our hard-working
citizens are filled with worry.

131
00:08:44,720 --> 00:08:46,240
I can lift their spirits!

132
00:08:46,540 --> 00:08:47,640
I will!

133
00:08:47,880 --> 00:08:50,800
By building our good people a Sea Train!

134
00:08:53,360 --> 00:08:55,889
Quit flapping your gums
and move your feet!

135
00:08:56,040 --> 00:08:57,040
No, let him stay.

136
00:08:58,120 --> 00:08:59,120
Sea Train.

137
00:08:59,720 --> 00:09:00,860
Tell me more.

138
00:09:01,100 --> 00:09:05,700
It's like a ship, but one that
puffs out steam and runs on a track.

139
00:09:06,080 --> 00:09:10,057
It'll go between the islands, carrying
people and all kinds of goods,

140
00:09:10,140 --> 00:09:11,140
even other ships.

141
00:09:11,480 --> 00:09:14,757
Most importantly, it won't be
affected by conditions at sea.

142
00:09:14,840 --> 00:09:15,899
That's ridiculous.

143
00:09:16,600 --> 00:09:20,577
A railway on the water will be ripped
to pieces once Aqualaguna comes around.

144
00:09:20,660 --> 00:09:24,257
And even if it doesn't, what are you going
to do about all the sea kings out there?

145
00:09:24,340 --> 00:09:26,837
It doesn't have to be a
completely fixed track.

146
00:09:26,920 --> 00:09:27,750
Huh?

147
00:09:27,833 --> 00:09:32,080
It'll be submerged under the water a bit,
so it won't be bombarded by the waves.

148
00:09:32,300 --> 00:09:34,757
It'll sway, just like a rope in the water.

149
00:09:34,840 --> 00:09:38,837
The Sea Train will just use the tracks
as a guide to get from place to place.

150
00:09:38,920 --> 00:09:42,497
I'm also considering installing
a mechanism that emits a loud,

151
00:09:42,580 --> 00:09:46,857
dissonant sound underwater to discourage
fish from getting anywhere near the tracks.

152
00:09:46,940 --> 00:09:50,237
It should work on sea kings as
well, so they won't pose a threat.

153
00:09:50,320 --> 00:09:51,908
Whoa, is all that possible?

154
00:09:52,300 --> 00:09:53,520
If we connect St.

155
00:09:53,660 --> 00:09:54,560
Poplar, Pucci,

156
00:09:54,920 --> 00:09:56,680
Sanfaldo, and this island,

157
00:09:56,900 --> 00:10:00,488
we can create a booming economy
that will help out all of us.

158
00:10:01,000 --> 00:10:01,830
Amazing.

159
00:10:02,020 --> 00:10:04,617
I will be finished with
the blueprints very soon,

160
00:10:04,700 --> 00:10:07,457
but it will take a master
shipwright to build it.

161
00:10:07,540 --> 00:10:10,277
Now, could the Sea Train run
to Annie's lobby as well?

162
00:10:10,360 --> 00:10:12,007
Without a doubt, Your Honor.

163
00:10:13,800 --> 00:10:17,447
Once the plans are in the can
and the railway is in the water,

164
00:10:17,660 --> 00:10:21,017
people can go with gusto from
island to island for work or play.

165
00:10:21,100 --> 00:10:25,440
And once again, Water 7 will
be a city filled with hope.

166
00:10:26,160 --> 00:10:27,600
How long will it take?

167
00:10:28,020 --> 00:10:28,940
Ten years.

168
00:10:29,480 --> 00:10:30,310
Then build it.

169
00:10:30,740 --> 00:10:35,140
If you agree to develop this Sea Train,
I will give you the time to do it.

170
00:10:35,360 --> 00:10:37,920
Consider these next
ten years as probation.

171
00:10:40,020 --> 00:10:41,300
That's great news.

172
00:10:41,580 --> 00:10:42,620
Good luck, Tom.

173
00:10:43,520 --> 00:10:45,400
Save Water 7, please.

174
00:10:49,860 --> 00:10:50,690
Ah, gusto.

175
00:10:50,880 --> 00:10:51,710
I'm alive!

176
00:10:51,860 --> 00:10:53,917
I'm glad you think this is so funny.

177
00:10:54,000 --> 00:10:55,157
I thought you were a goner.

178
00:10:55,240 --> 00:10:56,887
I was worried sick over you.

179
00:10:57,080 --> 00:10:59,157
But I guess if this
plan of yours works out,

180
00:10:59,240 --> 00:11:02,097
they're willing to forgive and
forget the whole Gold Roger affair.

181
00:11:02,180 --> 00:11:05,017
Well, I just got to tell you
how amazed I am with you, Tom.

182
00:11:05,100 --> 00:11:06,117
What a great idea!

183
00:11:06,200 --> 00:11:09,217
It's unbelievable to think you could
just come up with that on your own.

184
00:11:09,300 --> 00:11:11,124
It's brilliant when you told...

185
00:11:11,280 --> 00:11:12,197
Thanks for the grub.

186
00:11:12,280 --> 00:11:13,117
Come on, Yokozuna.

187
00:11:13,200 --> 00:11:15,024
I'll teach you the front crawl.

188
00:11:15,520 --> 00:11:18,157
Hey, we're all celebrating
here, and you want to leave?

189
00:11:18,240 --> 00:11:19,070
What's your deal?

190
00:11:19,153 --> 00:11:19,983
My deal?

191
00:11:20,220 --> 00:11:22,157
What happened to Tom was so unfair!

192
00:11:22,240 --> 00:11:25,357
He built the only ship that was
able to sail the whole Grand Line,

193
00:11:25,440 --> 00:11:27,457
something no one else
in the world could do!

194
00:11:27,540 --> 00:11:29,897
And those jerks want to
put him to death over it?

195
00:11:29,980 --> 00:11:32,077
They don't realize how hard that is!

196
00:11:32,160 --> 00:11:35,177
They couldn't even string together a
raft if their lives depended on it!

197
00:11:35,260 --> 00:11:36,090
I mean,

198
00:11:36,173 --> 00:11:38,317
I know that the whole reason our
office is under this bridge is

199
00:11:38,400 --> 00:11:41,517
because those stupid people kicked
you out of town over that ship!

200
00:11:41,600 --> 00:11:43,297
You're the greatest
shipbuilder the world has

201
00:11:43,380 --> 00:11:45,909
ever known and they
treat you like garbage!

202
00:11:47,060 --> 00:11:49,497
What are you laughing at,
you big yellow weirdo?

203
00:11:49,580 --> 00:11:50,410
You're crazy!

204
00:11:50,493 --> 00:11:52,419
Stop attacking him, you stupid kid!

205
00:11:52,660 --> 00:11:55,013
Why does he have to laugh at everything?

206
00:11:58,280 --> 00:11:59,380
No, no, no!

207
00:11:59,500 --> 00:12:00,794
You're doing it wrong!

208
00:12:01,860 --> 00:12:04,154
Stroke harder and push that water back!

209
00:12:06,780 --> 00:12:09,320
No, no! Do it harder! Don't hold back!

210
00:12:09,760 --> 00:12:11,537
That Frankie's got a lot of nerve.

211
00:12:11,620 --> 00:12:13,817
If I were you, I'd kick him
out for what he just did.

212
00:12:13,900 --> 00:12:16,135
Well, I know the boy can be a handful,

213
00:12:16,340 --> 00:12:18,997
but he's a fellow shipbuilder
at his young age He's

214
00:12:19,080 --> 00:12:22,117
almost on par with the best
craftsman on the island.

215
00:12:22,200 --> 00:12:24,000
He does build battleships.

216
00:12:24,180 --> 00:12:25,010
Yeah

217
00:12:25,100 --> 00:12:27,480
His problem is he's too honest.

218
00:12:32,700 --> 00:12:35,557
Two years ago, I met that
kid on Scrap Heap Island.

219
00:12:35,640 --> 00:12:38,317
He'd gone there to collect
junk to make a cannon.

220
00:12:38,400 --> 00:12:40,260
It was firing it with Gusto

221
00:12:40,960 --> 00:12:43,040
Old guy! Hey! Help me out!

222
00:12:43,180 --> 00:12:45,474
My good-for-nothing parents ditched me!

223
00:12:45,720 --> 00:12:48,897
Apparently his folks couldn't
handle his rambunctious behavior,

224
00:12:48,980 --> 00:12:50,617
so they threw him off their ship.

225
00:12:50,700 --> 00:12:53,759
Sounds like a couple of
heartless pirates to me, eh?

226
00:12:54,180 --> 00:12:55,300
What a joke!

227
00:12:56,020 --> 00:12:57,000
No, Tom.

228
00:12:57,580 --> 00:12:59,140
He is one tough kid.

229
00:12:59,400 --> 00:13:02,377
He's had a rough go at it, but
he's still got a good heart.

230
00:13:02,460 --> 00:13:04,697
I'm positive that both
of you boys are going to

231
00:13:04,780 --> 00:13:07,237
grow up to be world-class
shipwrights someday.

232
00:13:07,320 --> 00:13:08,897
There's no need for you to be rivals.

233
00:13:08,980 --> 00:13:10,577
I don't know about all that.

234
00:13:10,660 --> 00:13:13,425
It's like he's allergic
to sanity or something.

235
00:13:13,540 --> 00:13:14,370
Well,

236
00:13:14,453 --> 00:13:18,157
I just need to finish those blueprints and
then we'll build ourselves a Sea Train.

237
00:13:18,240 --> 00:13:20,520
Yeah, I bet he won't help at all.

238
00:13:21,480 --> 00:13:23,640
He can do whatever he wants.

239
00:13:42,800 --> 00:13:45,600
Thank you.

240
00:14:12,680 --> 00:14:15,480
Thank you.

241
00:15:01,760 --> 00:15:02,590
Suicide?

242
00:15:02,900 --> 00:15:03,980
That's the word.

243
00:15:04,220 --> 00:15:06,257
Head of the fourth largest shipyard.

244
00:15:06,340 --> 00:15:08,000
What a tragic story.

245
00:15:08,700 --> 00:15:12,117
They ran out of materials, so he took
a ship out to sea to get some more.

246
00:15:12,200 --> 00:15:13,980
Lost 50 men on the water.

247
00:15:14,980 --> 00:15:16,862
They had to close down his shop.

248
00:15:18,300 --> 00:15:19,220
Oh, man.

249
00:15:19,440 --> 00:15:21,020
Will this be how it ends?

250
00:15:21,320 --> 00:15:23,880
Is this how Water 7 finally dies?

251
00:15:25,040 --> 00:15:25,870
Hey!

252
00:15:25,953 --> 00:15:26,783
Did you guys hear?

253
00:15:26,866 --> 00:15:28,622
Big news from Scrap Heap Island!

254
00:15:30,300 --> 00:15:31,260
No way.

255
00:15:31,520 --> 00:15:32,620
Did they do it?

256
00:15:33,040 --> 00:15:36,180
Did Tom's workers actually
finish the Sea Train?

257
00:15:36,780 --> 00:15:37,610
Whoa!

